  "annotations": [
    {
      "id": "note-directions",
      "page": "page-1",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -230,
      "w": 700,
      "text": "Fifteen marks. The bottom row is the picture-frame-plus-data brief — start there if that is what you want to judge.\n\nEverything above it is the earlier exploration, all built on the same quality: mass. Every board says what it costs you as well as what it gives you."
    },
    {
      "id": "note-second-row",
      "page": "page-1",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 1010,
      "w": 700,
      "text": "Second set — the data itself, the frame with depth, and pure graphic abstraction."
    },
    {
      "id": "note-third-row",
      "page": "page-1",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 2250,
      "w": 700,
      "text": "Third set. Watching without the animal, the other half of the name cut out of solid ground, frames as layers, and the signal passing through."
    },
    {
      "id": "note-fourth-row",
      "page": "page-1",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 3490,
      "w": 700,
      "text": "Your brief: a picture frame and a data icon fused. Same chunky moulding on all four so they are judged on the data inside — a chart, a table, a trend line that will not stay in, and the database everyone already recognises."
    },
    {
      "id": "note-wordmarks",
      "page": "page-1",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 4730,
      "w": 700,
      "text": "The name as the logo. Four with some kind of border, four without — a full frame, a solid plaque, rules above and below, a data glyph for the hyphen, your own italic accent, a terminal prompt, a stacked imprint, and two corners doing the work of four."
    },
    {
      "id": "note-package",
      "page": "page-2",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -230,
      "w": 700,
      "text": "The reusable part — palette, type, spacing rules, and the pieces you would actually print or upload.\n\nThe mark shown throughout is an early placeholder, not a recommendation. Everything here rebuilds around whichever direction you pick."
    },
    {
      "id": "note-pieces",
      "page": "page-2",
      "x": 1120,
      "y": -230,
      "w": 620,
      "text": "These five are at true export sizes — the card is 3.5×2in, the avatar 400px, the banner is LinkedIn's 1584×396, the slide is 16:9.\n\nAnything in [square brackets] is a real fact I do not have."
    }
